# Line endings are normalized here so the repository holds one convention and
# an edit made on one platform never lands as a diff on another. Without this,
# a file written on Linux and committed from Windows can show up as a
# whole-file change that alters nothing but the bytes at the end of each line.
#
# text=auto lets Git decide what is text; eol=lf keeps LF in the working copy
# on every platform, including Windows. Modern Windows editors and tooling
# handle LF, and matching the repository avoids a class of diff that is noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vector databases and any binary output: never inspected or rewritten.
*.pkl binary

# guide.ipynb is redistributed from anthropics/claude-cookbooks unchanged, and
# the README says so. Normalization would rewrite its bytes and quietly make
# that claim false, so it is excluded from the text rules entirely.
*.ipynb -text
